# Toleration Demo

This folder shows how a pod can tolerate a taint on a node.

## What it does

The pod includes a `tolerations` section that allows it to schedule onto a node tainted with `NoSchedule`.

This is useful when a workload must run on a control-plane or specially tainted node even though the node is intentionally marked to reject most workloads.

## Example purpose

- keep the pod on a tainted node
- allow control-plane scheduling for debugging or cluster services
- demonstrate node affinity with tolerations
